Task: Phase 4c — TV navigation and presentation repair (FR-11).

Why: the owner reports the TV client as "awful and not navigable". The
investigation (commit 8895cfb) named 16 findings; this implements the fix.

Navigation (F1-F5, new F17):
- Deleted the bare Focus row wrappers on Home and the search wrappers on
  Movies/Series. They were traversable stops with no focus cue, so every Down
  press landed on them and then trapped at the last row.
- NetflixScaffold.root is now non-traversable (it stranded focus on Movies and
  Series and then blocked Down).
- The search FocusNodes are bound to the TextField, so the input method
  attaches and the fields accept text (F5).
- LeanbackScaffold now owns the rail boundary (F17, found while implementing):
  each routed page sits in its own ModalRoute FocusScope, and Flutter's
  directional traversal only searches the focused node's enclosingScope, so the
  rail was unreachable from the content in the production router shell. Left at
  a row's left edge opens the rail and focuses the current destination; Right on
  the rail returns to the item the user came from; the other row edges do
  nothing.
- FocusableAction reveals itself in every enclosing Scrollable
  (keepVisibleAtStart: no-op when already visible).

Controls and presentation (F6-F8, F11-F16):
- Recently Added activation wired (it was an empty closure with a false comment).
- Continue Watching cards show artwork and use one focus cue.
- One focus cue (FocusableAction) on ActionBar, MediaHero actions, episode
  actions, the rail, and the subtitle search. FocusableCard deleted.
- Focus pop grows into reserved padding instead of a Matrix4 transform, so the
  ring is never clipped and neighbours never move.
- Hero: real backdrop (Movie.fanartUrl) or a designed gradient plus a poster
  tile; portrait posters are never cropped into the banner.
- Year printed once; FileInfoCard hides a zero size; playback title uses SxxExx.
- Detail screens push on the root navigator with a large focused Back control;
  episode rows are width-constrained to 1100 px.
- TV type and tile scale (28px titles, 18px+ body, 32px rail icons, 240px tiles).
- Deleted five unreachable screens, three dead widgets, three sheets, and their
  ten test files (F7). The rail keeps Home/Movies/Series (owner-approved strip)
  and gains a Server affordance that opens /discovery?switch=1.

Tests (F9):
- home_screen_dpad_test.dart rewritten to mount the real HomeScreen (the
  _DpadHomeProbe mock is deleted, along with its conditional assertion).
- library_dpad_test.dart added for MoviesScreen/SeriesScreen.
- test/support/focus_probe.dart provides expectVisibleFocus: after every key
  press focus must sit on a control that renders a focus cue.

Gates: flutter analyze clean; flutter test 320 passed.
